		<readme>docs\README.md</readme>
		<description>IronSoftware.System.Drawing - The C# Image Library

A universally compatible Bitmap format for .NET 8, .NET 7, .NET 6, and .NET 5, .NET Core on Windows, macOS, Linux, Docker, AWS, Azure, NanoServer, IIS, Mobile, Xamarin, iOS, Android, and Google Compute.

Works seamlessly with popular Image and Bitmap formats such as System.Drawing.Bitmap, SkiaSharp, SixLabors.ImageSharp, Microsoft.Maui.Graphics.

Implicit casting means that using this class to input and output Bitmap and image types from public API's gives full compatibility to all image type fully supported by Microsoft.

Key library features include:
* AnyBitmap: A universally compatible Bitmap class. Implicit casting between System.Drawing.Bitmap, System.Drawing.Image, SkiaSharp.SKBitmap, SkiaSharp.SKImage, SixLabors.ImageSharp, Microsoft.Maui.Graphics.Platform.PlatformImage to IronSoftware.Drawing.AnyBitmap
* Color: A universally compatible Color class. Implicit casting between System.Drawing.Color, SkiaSharp.SKColor, SixLabors.ImageSharp.Color, SixLabors.ImageSharp.PixelFormats to IronSoftware.Drawing.Color
* Rectangle: A universally compatible Rectangle class. Implicit casting between System.Drawing.Rectangle, SkiaSharp.SKRect, SkiaSharp.SKRectI, SixLabors.ImageSharp.Rectangle to IronSoftware.Drawing.Rectangle
* Font: A universally compatible Font class. Implicit casting between System.Drawing.Font, SkiaSharp.SKFont, SixLabors.Fonts.Font to IronSoftware.Drawing.Font
* Point: A universally compatible Point class. Implicit casting between System.Drawing.Point, SixLabors.ImageSharp.Point, SkiaSharp.SKPointI to IronSoftware.Drawing.Point
* Size: A universally compatible Size class. Implicit casting between System.Drawing.Size, SixLabors.ImageSharp.Size, SkiaSharp.SKSizeI to IronSoftware.Drawing.Size

IronSoftware.Drawing can be used within C#, VB.NET, F#, ASP.NET projects, MVC, Web Services, Console &amp; Desktop Applications.

Supports:
* .NET 9
* .NET 8
* .NET 7
* .NET 6
* .NET 5
* .NET Core 2.0 +
* .NET Framework 4.6.2 +

For general support and technical inquiries, please email us at: support@ironsoftware.com</description>
		<summary>IronSoftware.System.Drawing is an open-source solution for .NET developers to replace System.Drawing.Common with a universal and flexible library.</summary>
		<releaseNotes>
Breaking Changes
- .NET Framework 4.6.2+ now has its own build that no longer depends on SixLabors.ImageSharp (2.x is end-of-life and no longer receives security fixes). Images are decoded, processed and encoded with SkiaSharp 4.153.1 and BitMiracle.LibTiff.NET instead
- On .NET Framework the implicit conversions between IronSoftware.Drawing types (AnyBitmap, Color, Point, PointF, Rectangle, RectangleF, Size, SizeF, CropRectangle) and SixLabors.ImageSharp types are no longer available. Libraries compiled against an earlier IronSoftware.System.Drawing that use those conversions must be rebuilt for .NET Framework
- On .NET Framework, SVG loading uses Svg.Skia 5.2.3 instead of SkiaSharp.Svg 1.60 (which does not work with SkiaSharp 4); install Svg.Skia to load SVG files
Features
- Added a .NET 8 target using ImageSharp 4.1.3 and Drawing 3.1.3, enabling security fixes including CVE-2026-106114.
- Updated SixLabors.ImageSharp to 3.2.0 (Drawing 2.2.0) for .NET 6 and 4.1.3 (Drawing 3.1.3) for .NET 8. .NET Standard 2.0 stays on 2.1.13.
Security
- .NET Standard 2.0: AnyBitmap now rejects malformed BigTIFF files that make ImageSharp 2.1.13 loop forever (CVE-2026-106116). .NET Framework decodes TIFF with BitMiracle.LibTiff.NET and is not affected.
- Added ImageSharpLoader (.NET Standard 2.0, .NET 6, .NET 8), a drop-in replacement for SixLabors.ImageSharp Image.Load that applies the same check. Use it instead of Image.Load on untrusted data. It is not available on .NET Framework, which has no ImageSharp dependency.
Dependencies
- .NET Framework: SkiaSharp 4.153.1 and SixLabors.Fonts 1.0.0 are now declared dependencies; SixLabors.ImageSharp and SixLabors.ImageSharp.Drawing are no longer required
- .NET Standard 2.0 / .NET Framework: System.Memory 4.6.3, System.Buffers 4.6.1, System.Numerics.Vectors 4.6.1 and System.Runtime.CompilerServices.Unsafe 6.1.2 are now declared dependencies. .NET Framework apps need binding redirects to System.Memory 4.0.5.0, System.Buffers 4.0.5.0, System.Numerics.Vectors 4.1.6.0 and System.Runtime.CompilerServices.Unsafe 6.0.3.0; SDK-style and PackageReference projects generate these automatically
		</releaseNotes>
